  "_readme": "Maintainable, INDEPENDENT pricing table for estimating USD cost of Copilot model usage. These are NOT official GitHub Copilot prices (Copilot bills via premium requests/AIUs, not raw token USD) — they are best-effort public list-price approximations for the underlying model family, used only to produce a rough, independent USD estimate. Prices are USD per 1,000,000 tokens. 'reasoning tokens' are a SUBSET of output/completion tokens (not billed separately/again) and are charged at output_per_million. 'cache_read_per_million' prices the subset of input tokens served from a prompt cache (also a SUBSET of input tokens, not additional tokens); if omitted for a model, cache-read tokens are estimated at the full input_per_million rate. Add/edit entries as models change; add an alias in \"aliases\" pointing at an entry key (or null to mark it explicitly-unpriced) if Copilot/OTEL exposes a model under a different id/spelling than the entries below — alias resolution is recursive (alias -> alias -> model) with a cycle guard. Unknown models with no matching entry or alias are deliberately left unpriced (omitted) so the report can show an explicit 'no pricing data' notice instead of silently reporting $0.",
